 # Stream Lines
 
-Also called: Integral Curve, Stream Lines and Ribbons Rendering
+Also called: Integral Curve, Particle Tracer, Stream Lines and Ribbons Rendering
 
 ## Overview
-Stream lines are a local point tracking algorithm that visualizes vector fields by computing curves tangent to the field at every point, approximating the path of an infinitesimal massless particle [S1, S3, S6, unofficial]. Unlike [Glyph-based Vector/Tensor Visualization](10535-glyph-based-vector-tensor-visualization.md), which displays discrete vectors at fixed grid locations, stream lines reveal continuous flow topology and connectivity [S9, unofficial]. They differ from [Stream Surfaces](7696-stream-surfaces.md) by representing individual trajectories rather than surfaces formed by families of lines [S1, unofficial].
+Stream lines are a local point tracking algorithm that visualizes vector fields by computing curves tangent to the field at every point, approximating the path of an infinitesimal massless particle [S1, S3, S6, unofficial]. Unlike [Glyph-based Vector/Tensor Visualization](10535-glyph-based-vector-tensor-visualization.md), which displays discrete vectors at fixed grid locations, stream lines reveal continuous flow topology and connectivity [S10, unofficial]. They differ from [Stream Surfaces](7696-stream-surfaces.md) by representing individual trajectories rather than surfaces formed by families of lines [S1, unofficial].
 
